{"id": "EUVD-2026-90435", "enisaUuid": "d626bd5e-a0f0-338b-82ec-04bb428e49be", "description": "QloApps through 1.7.0 contains a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability in the back-office Hotel Reservation System Book Now search, where date_to and id_room_type parameters are copied into template variables without validation. Attackers can craft a malicious link containing JavaScript payload in these parameters that executes in an authenticated administrator's session when the victim follows the link.", "datePublished": "2026-09-30T23:02:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T13:36:56", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/pull/1884", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/commit/1d06fd302a935d68203dbdb341d89482621769d7", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/modules/hotelreservationsystem/controllers/admin/AdminHotelRoomsBookingController.php", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/modules/hotelreservationsystem/views/templates/admin/hotel_rooms_booking/helpers/view/_partials/booking-rooms.tpl", "https://hackmd.io/@leediay/reflected-xss-qloapps-via-booking-now", "https://hackmd.io/@leediay/four-reflected-xss-qloapps", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/qloapps-through-1.7.0-reflected-xss-via-book-now-search-parameters"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-103587", "GHSA-cw3f-pcq3-9hrw"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c23faaab-1860-3a05-9236-b3a625db8075", "product": {"name": "QloApps", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "338f9b0c-cb45-3092-9225-f03f71c2d186", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}], "isExploited": false}